// file makes that §8 leaves open: docs/adr/0007-engine-renders-a-render-plan.md (what a plan
// is), 0008 (how it travels, and what the engine reports), 0009 §2 (what the hash is of).
//
// The engine never receives a Song. It receives a RenderPlan: flat, ordered, already
// resolved. Nothing that needs the model's structure crosses — no id-keyed map, no
// Clip.track_id, no Mix.solo to resolve against other tracks, no loop_length_ticks to expand,
// no Effect.index to sort by, no history field. Core does all of that once, in compile, and
// the engine renders exactly length_ticks ticks with no opinion of its own (ADR 0007 §1).
